        337.43896484375,
        131.98500061035156,
        478.5346374511719,
        141.74598693847656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Different SPC algorithms arise from various choices of",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629638671875,
        146.29443359375,
        558.0014038085938,
        155.20098876953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "g(·). For instance, MPPI [16] uses a Boltzmann-like expo-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        157.53311157226562,
        558.0011596679688,
        167.156982421875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "nentially weighted average,",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        170.2054443359375,
        424.6813659667969,
        179.11199951171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gMP P I(J) = exp (−J/λ) ,",
      "bbox": [
        380.0999450683594,
        188.59512329101562,
        491.1226501464844,
        198.9140167236328
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(6)",
      "bbox": [
        546.4050903320312,
        189.31243896484375,
        558.0215454101562,
        198.218994140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where λ > 0 is the temperature parameter. A smaller λ",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        208.26002502441406,
        557.9910278320312,
        217.32598876953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gives more weight to the lowest-cost samples. In the low-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        220.37445068359375,
        558.0009155273438,
        229.281005859375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "temperature limit we recover predictive sampling [17],",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        232.2099151611328,
        542.0408935546875,
        241.23602294921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gP S(J) = lim",
      "bbox": [
        377.5949401855469,
        251.2770538330078,
        437.0224304199219,
        261.03802490234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "λ→0 exp (−J/λ) ,",
      "bbox": [
        421.7769470214844,
        250.71914672851562,
        493.615966796875,
        266.6268310546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(7)",
      "bbox": [
        546.3978271484375,
        251.43646240234375,
        558.0142822265625,
        260.343017578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where the updated mean ¯U is simply chosen as the lowest-",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        271.5850524902344,
        557.9998779296875,
        283.16900634765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "cost sample. Another popular option is CEM [18], [22],",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999206542969,
        286.0978698730469,
        558.0009155273438,
        295.1239929199219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which weighs the top performing samples equally,",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999206542969,
        298.17242431640625,
        519.6946411132812,
        307.0789794921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gCEM(J) =",
      "bbox": [
        374.01092529296875,
        324.75701904296875,
        424.79803466796875,
        334.5179443359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(",
      "bbox": [
        427.55596923828125,
        314.2355651855469,
        435.5858154296875,
        320.61163330078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "bbox": [
        435.5809631347656,
        317.9620361328125,
        440.562255859375,
        326.8088073730469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "if J ≤γ",
      "bbox": [
        450.52484130859375,
        317.40411376953125,
        485.5334167480469,
        326.8088073730469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "0",
      "bbox": [
        435.5809631347656,
        332.30804443359375,
        440.562255859375,
        341.1548156738281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "otherwise .",
      "bbox": [
        450.52484130859375,
        324.7570495605469,
        497.1915588378906,
        341.1548156738281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(8)",
      "bbox": [
        546.3869018554688,
        324.91644287109375,
        558.0033569335938,
        333.822998046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The threshold γ is defined implicitly by a user-selected",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        351.1560363769531,
        558.0008544921875,
        360.22198486328125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "number of elite samples. CEM is typically paired with",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        363.2704162597656,
        558.0009155273438,
        372.1769714355469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "an adaptive update rule for the variance of the proposal",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        375.2264099121094,
        558.0009765625,
        384.1329650878906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "distribution. Tsallis-MPPI [31] provides a middle ground",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        387.06182861328125,
        558.0009155273438,
        396.08795166015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "between MPPI and CEM via a generalized exponential,",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        399.1363830566406,
        541.3733520507812,
        408.0429382324219
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gT MP P I(J) = max(1 −(r −1)J/λ, 0)",
      "bbox": [
        345.365966796875,
        417.9180603027344,
        507.89605712890625,
        428.2369079589844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1",
      "bbox": [
        513.5260009765625,
        414.9529724121094,
        516.9182739257812,
        419.3763732910156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "r−1 ,",
      "bbox": [
        509.0690002441406,
        416.5729675292969,
        525.8355712890625,
        427.32275390625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(9)",
      "bbox": [
        546.388427734375,
        418.6353759765625,
        558.0048828125,
        427.54193115234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where the original MPPI update is recovered as r →1.",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        437.0250549316406,
        540.0681762695312,
        446.64892578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The ability to parallelize rollouts (4) is a key advantage",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629943847656,
        449.7933654785156,
        558.0013427734375,
        458.6999206542969
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "over gradient-based MPC, an advantage that is further re-",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        461.74835205078125,
        558.0010375976562,
        470.6549072265625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "inforced by massively parallel GPU simulators [19]–[21].",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        473.7033386230469,
        558.0011596679688,
        482.6098937988281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Sampling can also reduce the severity of local minima and",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        485.6593322753906,
        558.0009765625,
        494.5658874511719
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "smooth out stiff dynamics associated with contact [32], [33].",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        497.61431884765625,
        558.0010986328125,
        506.5208740234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "B. Generative Modeling",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        517.2000122070312,
        412.5469970703125,
        525.7877807617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Generative modeling considers a seemingly different prob-",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629943847656,
        532.540283203125,
        558.00146484375,
        541.4468383789062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "lem: produce a sample x from a probability distribution p(x).",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        544.3358764648438,
        558.0007934570312,
        553.40185546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "In the typical setting, we do not have access to p(x) in closed",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        556.2908935546875,
        558.0009765625,
        565.3568725585938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "form, but we do have samples (training data) from p(x).",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        568.2459106445312,
        546.005859375,
        577.3118896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "1) Flow Matching: Flow matching [7] is based on the idea",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629943847656,
        580.5053100585938,
        558.0013427734375,
        589.411865234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of a probability density path pt(x). This path flows from an",
      "bbox": [
        313.1999816894531,
        592.3009033203125,
        558.0028686523438,
        602.0618896484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "easy-to-sample distribution p0(x) = N(0, I) at t = 0 to the",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        603.6980590820312,
        558.0140380859375,
        614.016845703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "data distribution at t = 1. Flow matching methods learn a",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        616.2109375,
        558.0009155273438,
        625.2769165039062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "vector field vθ(x, t) that moves samples along this path.",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        628.1658935546875,
        543.6564331054688,
        637.9278564453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The flow network vθ is trained via standard (stochastic)",
      "bbox": [
        323.1629638671875,
        640.2178955078125,
        558.0017700195312,
        650.7778930664062
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "gradient descent methods on",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        652.3323364257812,
        429.9117431640625,
        661.2388916015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "min",
      "bbox": [
        368.33795166015625,
        671.2799072265625,
        384.94561767578125,
        680.126708984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "θ",
      "bbox": [
        374.6359558105469,
        679.8571166992188,
        378.4297180175781,
        686.0498657226562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Et,x0,x1 [LF M(θ; x0, x1, t)] ,",
      "bbox": [
        386.60296630859375,
        670.7220458984375,
        502.865234375,
        682.61669921875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(10)",
      "bbox": [
        541.4105224609375,
        671.4393310546875,
        558.00830078125,
        680.3458862304688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "where θ are learnable parameters (e.g., network weights) and",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        692.8499145507812,
        558.0010375976562,
        701.9158935546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "LF M (θ; x0, x1, t) =",
      "bbox": [
        313.199951171875,
        712.1000366210938,
        397.8318176269531,
        722.9987182617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
